Falsifies `dma_validator::the_outer_walk_stays_inside_the_rings_and_terminates`.

The defect: `validate_and_shadow` no longer refuses a head index that names a slot
outside the descriptor table. The head is a `u16` the driver writes into its own
available ring, so this is attacker-chosen, and without the guard the walk reads
descriptor `head` at `driver_desc + head * 16`, up to a megabyte past the table
the driver was granted. The confinement checks that follow are unaffected and
still run; they run on bytes read from outside the ring.

Expected to fail: the read closure's `assert!(off < 16 * QS as u64, "a descriptor
read past the end of the table")`. The harness models the ring's bounds in its
closures rather than in its body, so that assertion is where this property is
actually stated. Confirmed: one failing check, located in this harness's
`read64` closure at the line holding that assertion.

